IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Crimes Act 1914 (Commonwealth), sections 4AA to 4N -- the module that
-- counts and compares periods, dates and amounts.
--
-- It imports only `prelude` and `daydate`, and every other module of this
-- encoding calls it for each number, term of imprisonment, date and age the
-- text states or implies.
--
-- Dates are written `Date day month year`, never with a year-first
-- constructor. `Date` rolls an impossible date forward (`Date 31 6 2026` is
-- 1 July 2026), so no date built here is ever a 31st of a 30-day month or a
-- 29 February of a year that has none. `add years` from a 29 February
-- clamps to 28 February, which this module does not use: where a rule turns
-- on a 29 February start it says so in its own comment.
--
-- Money is a NUMBER of dollars; a count of penalty units is a NUMBER of
-- penalty units; a period of imprisonment is an ImprisonmentTerm.

§ `Crimes Act 1914 (Cth) ss 4AA-4N: periods, dates and amounts`

§§ `Terms of imprisonment`

-- A maximum term of imprisonment, as the text states it: in months (s 4B(2),
-- s 4G, s 4H, s 4J(3)(a)) or in years (s 4J(1), s 4J(3)), for life (s 4B(2A))
-- or not at all (s 4H(b)).
DECLARE ImprisonmentTerm IS ONE OF
    Months HAS months IS A NUMBER
    Years HAS years IS A NUMBER
    ForLife
    NoImprisonment

-- The bands into which the text's thresholds of 12 months, 5 years and 10
-- years cut a term of imprisonment.
DECLARE TermBand IS ONE OF
    `not punishable by imprisonment`
    `12 months or less`
    `more than 12 months but not more than 5 years`
    `more than 5 years but not more than 10 years`
    `more than 10 years`

-- src:4375 | Term of Imprisonment is the maximum term of imprisonment, expressed in months, by which the offence is punishable.
@ref s 4B(2) (src:4375)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of months in a year` MEANS 12

-- src:4375 | Term of Imprisonment is the maximum term of imprisonment, expressed in months, by which the offence is punishable.
@ref s 4B(2) (src:4375)
GIVEN `the term` IS AN ImprisonmentTerm
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the term of imprisonment expressed in months` IS
    CONSIDER `the term`
    WHEN Months m THEN IF m GREATER THAN 0 THEN JUST m ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN Years y THEN IF y GREATER THAN 0 THEN JUST (y TIMES `the number of months in a year`) ELSE NOTHING
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:4409 | Offences against a law of the Commonwealth punishable by imprisonment for a period exceeding 12 months are indictable offences, unless the contrary intention appears.
@ref s 4G (src:4409)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of months in 12 months` MEANS 12

-- src:4419 | (a) where the offence is punishable by imprisonment for a period not exceeding 5 years—a sentence of imprisonment for a period not exceeding 12 months or a fine not exceeding 60 penalty units, or both; or
@ref s 4J(3)(a) (src:4419)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of months in 5 years` MEANS 5 TIMES `the number of months in a year`

-- src:4416 | (1) Subject to subsection (2), an indictable offence (other than an offence referred to in subsection (4)) against a law of the Commonwealth, being an offence punishable by imprisonment for a period not exceeding 10 years, may, unless the contrary intention appears, be heard and determined, with the consent of the prosecutor and the defendant, by a court of summary jurisdiction.
@ref s 4J(1) (src:4416)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of months in 10 years` MEANS 10 TIMES `the number of months in a year`

-- src:4409 | Offences against a law of the Commonwealth punishable by imprisonment for a period exceeding 12 months are indictable offences, unless the contrary intention appears.
@ref s 4G (src:4409)
GIVEN `the term` IS AN ImprisonmentTerm
GIVETH A MAYBE TermBand
DECIDE `the band of a term of imprisonment` IS
    CONSIDER `the term`
    WHEN NoImprisonment THEN JUST `not punishable by imprisonment`
    WHEN ForLife THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE CONSIDER `the term of imprisonment expressed in months` `the term`
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
              WHEN JUST m THEN BRANCH IF m AT MOST `the number of months in 12 months` THEN JUST `12 months or less`
                                      IF m AT MOST `the number of months in 5 years` THEN JUST `more than 12 months but not more than 5 years`
                                      IF m AT MOST `the number of months in 10 years` THEN JUST `more than 5 years but not more than 10 years`
                                      OTHERWISE JUST `more than 10 years`

§§ `Penalty units and the indexation of the penalty unit (s 4AA)`

-- src:4338 | penalty unit means the amount of $330 (subject to indexation under subsection (3)).
@ref s 4AA(1) (src:4338)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount of a penalty unit before any indexation, in dollars` MEANS 330

-- src:4346 | (3) On 1 July 2026 and each third 1 July following that day (an indexation day), the dollar amount mentioned in subsection (1) is replaced by the amount worked out using the following formula:
@ref s 4AA(3) (src:4346)
GIVETH A DATE
`the first indexation day` MEANS Date 1 7 2026

-- src:4346 | (3) On 1 July 2026 and each third 1 July following that day (an indexation day), the dollar amount mentioned in subsection (1) is replaced by the amount worked out using the following formula:
@ref s 4AA(3) (src:4346)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of years from one indexation day to the next` MEANS 3

-- src:4346 | (3) On 1 July 2026 and each third 1 July following that day (an indexation day), the dollar amount mentioned in subsection (1) is replaced by the amount worked out using the following formula:
@ref s 4AA(3) (src:4346)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the indexation day numbered` IS
    Date 1 7 (DATE_YEAR `the first indexation day` PLUS (n TIMES `the number of years from one indexation day to the next`))

-- src:4346 | (3) On 1 July 2026 and each third 1 July following that day (an indexation day), the dollar amount mentioned in subsection (1) is replaced by the amount worked out using the following formula:
@ref s 4AA(3) (src:4346)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a day is an indexation day` IF
        DATE_DAY d EQUALS 1
    AND DATE_MONTH d EQUALS 7
    AND DATE_YEAR d AT LEAST DATE_YEAR `the first indexation day`
    AND ((DATE_YEAR d MINUS DATE_YEAR `the first indexation day`) MODULO `the number of years from one indexation day to the next`) EQUALS 0

-- src:4346 | (3) On 1 July 2026 and each third 1 July following that day (an indexation day), the dollar amount mentioned in subsection (1) is replaced by the amount worked out using the following formula:
@ref s 4AA(3) (src:4346)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the number of indexation days on or before` IS
    IF Day d LESS THAN Day `the first indexation day`
    THEN 0
    ELSE FLOOR ((DATE_YEAR d MINUS DATE_YEAR `the first indexation day`) DIVIDED BY `the number of years from one indexation day to the next`) PLUS
         IF Day d AT LEAST Day (`the indexation day numbered` (FLOOR ((DATE_YEAR d MINUS DATE_YEAR `the first indexation day`) DIVIDED BY `the number of years from one indexation day to the next`))) THEN 1 ELSE 0

-- src:146 | quarter means a period of 3 months ending on 31 March, 30 June, 30 September or 31 December.
@ref s 3(1) quarter (src:146)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a quarter ends on` IF
        (DATE_DAY d EQUALS 31 AND DATE_MONTH d EQUALS 3)
     OR (DATE_DAY d EQUALS 30 AND DATE_MONTH d EQUALS 6)
     OR (DATE_DAY d EQUALS 30 AND DATE_MONTH d EQUALS 9)
     OR (DATE_DAY d EQUALS 31 AND DATE_MONTH d EQUALS 12)

-- src:146 | quarter means a period of 3 months ending on 31 March, 30 June, 30 September or 31 December.
@ref s 3(1) quarter (src:146)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `the first day of the quarter ending on` IS
    IF `a quarter ends on` d
    THEN JUST (Date 1 (DATE_MONTH d MINUS 2) (DATE_YEAR d))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4351 | March quarter means a quarter ending on 31 March.
@ref s 4AA(4) March quarter (src:4351)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a March quarter ends on` IF
    DATE_DAY d EQUALS 31 AND DATE_MONTH d EQUALS 3

-- src:4352 | reference quarter means the March quarter immediately before the indexation day.
@ref s 4AA(4) reference quarter (src:4352)
GIVEN `the indexation day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the day on which the reference quarter ends` IS
    IF Day `the indexation day` GREATER THAN Day (Date 31 3 (DATE_YEAR `the indexation day`))
    THEN Date 31 3 (DATE_YEAR `the indexation day`)
    ELSE Date 31 3 (DATE_YEAR `the indexation day` MINUS 1)

-- src:4349 | base quarter means the March quarter 3 years before the reference quarter.
@ref s 4AA(4) base quarter (src:4349)
GIVEN `the indexation day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the day on which the base quarter ends` IS
    Date 31 3 (DATE_YEAR (`the day on which the reference quarter ends` `the indexation day`) MINUS 3)

-- src:4353 | (5) An indexation factor is to be calculated to 3 decimal places (rounding up if the fourth decimal place is 5 or more).
@ref s 4AA(5) (src:4353)
GIVEN `the ratio` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `an indexation factor calculated to 3 decimal places` IS
    FLOOR ((`the ratio` TIMES 1000) PLUS 0.5) DIVIDED BY 1000

-- s 4AA(4): the formula in the text deposit's sidecar is
--   Index number for the reference quarter / Index number for the base quarter
-- (the sidecar is `C1914A00012.formulas.md`, entry s 4AA(4)).
-- src:4347 | (4) The indexation factor for an indexation day is the number worked out using the following formula:
-- src:4348 | where:
@ref s 4AA(4) (src:4347-4348)
GIVEN `the index number for the reference quarter` IS A NUMBER
      `the index number for the base quarter` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the indexation factor for an indexation day` IS
    IF `the index number for the base quarter` EQUALS 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`an indexation factor calculated to 3 decimal places` (`the index number for the reference quarter` DIVIDED BY `the index number for the base quarter`))

-- s 4AA(3): the formula in the sidecar (entry s 4AA(3)) is
--   Indexation factor for the indexation day x Dollar amount immediately before the indexation day
-- src:4354 | (6) Amounts worked out under subsection (3) are to be rounded to the nearest whole dollar (rounding 50 cents upwards).
@ref s 4AA(3), (6) (src:4354)
GIVEN `the indexation factor` IS A NUMBER
      `the dollar amount immediately before the indexation day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the dollar amount after an indexation, to the nearest whole dollar` IS
    FLOOR ((`the indexation factor` TIMES `the dollar amount immediately before the indexation day`) PLUS 0.5)

-- src:4359 | (8) If the dollar amount mentioned in subsection (1) is increased in accordance with subsection (3), the increased amount only applies to offences committed on or after the indexation day.
@ref s 4AA(8) (src:4359)
GIVEN `the day of the offence` IS A DATE
      `the indexation day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence was committed on or after the indexation day` IF
    Day `the day of the offence` AT LEAST Day `the indexation day`

§§ `Alterations in penalties, and the day of commencement (ss 4AA(8) and 4F)`

-- s 4F(1) and (2) speak of offences committed "after" and "before" the
-- commencement of a provision. The text does not say whether an offence
-- committed on the day of commencement is after the commencement, so a day
-- that is neither before nor after the commencement day is NOTHING.
-- src:4406 | (1) Where a provision of a law of the Commonwealth increases the penalty or maximum penalty for an offence, the penalty or maximum penalty as increased applies only to offences committed after the commencement of that provision.
@ref s 4F(1) (src:4406)
GIVEN `the day of the offence` IS A DATE
      `the day of commencement` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence was committed after the commencement` IS
    BRANCH IF Day `the day of the offence` GREATER THAN Day `the day of commencement` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF Day `the day of the offence` LESS THAN Day `the day of commencement` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:4407 | (2) Where a provision of a law of the Commonwealth reduces the penalty or maximum penalty for an offence, the penalty or maximum penalty as reduced extends to offences committed before the commencement of that provision, but the reduction does not affect any penalty imposed before that commencement.
@ref s 4F(2) (src:4407)
GIVEN `the day of the offence` IS A DATE
      `the day of commencement` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence was committed before the commencement` IS
    BRANCH IF Day `the day of the offence` LESS THAN Day `the day of commencement` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF Day `the day of the offence` GREATER THAN Day `the day of commencement` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- "any penalty imposed before that commencement": the same day arithmetic,
-- applied to the day the penalty was imposed. Imposed on the commencement
-- day itself is neither before nor after it, so NOTHING.
-- src:4407 | (2) Where a provision of a law of the Commonwealth reduces the penalty or maximum penalty for an offence, the penalty or maximum penalty as reduced extends to offences committed before the commencement of that provision, but the reduction does not affect any penalty imposed before that commencement.
@ref s 4F(2) (src:4407)
GIVEN `the day the penalty was imposed` IS A DATE
      `the day of commencement` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a penalty was imposed before the commencement` IS
    BRANCH IF Day `the day the penalty was imposed` LESS THAN Day `the day of commencement` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF Day `the day the penalty was imposed` GREATER THAN Day `the day of commencement` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Conversion of a penalty stated in dollars (s 4AB)`

-- src:4361 | (1) A reference in a law of the Commonwealth or in a Territory Ordinance to a pecuniary penalty of D dollars, where D is a number, is taken to be a reference to a pecuniary penalty of P penalty units, where P is:
-- src:4362 | (a) if D ÷ 100 is a whole number—that whole number; or
-- src:4363 | (b) if D ÷ 100 is not a whole number—the next highest whole number.
@ref s 4AB(1) (src:4361-4363)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of dollars to a penalty unit in a conversion` MEANS 100

-- src:4361 | (1) A reference in a law of the Commonwealth or in a Territory Ordinance to a pecuniary penalty of D dollars, where D is a number, is taken to be a reference to a pecuniary penalty of P penalty units, where P is:
-- src:4362 | (a) if D ÷ 100 is a whole number—that whole number; or
-- src:4363 | (b) if D ÷ 100 is not a whole number—the next highest whole number.
@ref s 4AB(1) (src:4361-4363)
GIVEN `D` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the number of penalty units that a penalty of D dollars is taken to be` IS
    IF FLOOR (`D` DIVIDED BY `the number of dollars to a penalty unit in a conversion`) EQUALS (`D` DIVIDED BY `the number of dollars to a penalty unit in a conversion`)
    THEN `D` DIVIDED BY `the number of dollars to a penalty unit in a conversion`
    ELSE FLOOR (`D` DIVIDED BY `the number of dollars to a penalty unit in a conversion`) PLUS 1

§§ `Maximum pecuniary penalties (s 4B)`

-- s 4B(2): the formula in the sidecar (entry s 4B(2)) is  Term of Imprisonment x 5
-- src:4373 | (2) Where a natural person is convicted of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth punishable by imprisonment only, the court may, if the contrary intention does not appear and the court thinks it appropriate in all the circumstances of the case, impose, instead of, or in addition to, a penalty of imprisonment, a pecuniary penalty not exceeding the number of penalty units calculated using the formula:
@ref s 4B(2) (src:4373)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of penalty units for each month of the maximum term, s 4B(2)` MEANS 5

-- src:4373 | (2) Where a natural person is convicted of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth punishable by imprisonment only, the court may, if the contrary intention does not appear and the court thinks it appropriate in all the circumstances of the case, impose, instead of, or in addition to, a penalty of imprisonment, a pecuniary penalty not exceeding the number of penalty units calculated using the formula:
@ref s 4B(2) (src:4373)
GIVEN `the term` IS AN ImprisonmentTerm
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the number of penalty units calculated using the formula` IS
    CONSIDER `the term of imprisonment expressed in months` `the term`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST m THEN JUST (m TIMES `the number of penalty units for each month of the maximum term, s 4B(2)`)

-- src:4376 | (2A) Where a natural person is convicted of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth in respect of which a court may impose a penalty of imprisonment for life, the court may, if the contrary intention does not appear and the court thinks it appropriate in all the circumstances of the case, impose, instead of, or in addition to, a penalty of imprisonment, a pecuniary penalty not exceeding 2,000 penalty units.
@ref s 4B(2A) (src:4376)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of penalty units for an offence punishable by imprisonment for life` MEANS 2000

-- src:4377 | (3) Where a body corporate is convicted of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth, the court may, if the contrary intention does not appear and the court thinks fit, impose a pecuniary penalty not exceeding an amount equal to 5 times the amount of the maximum pecuniary penalty that could be imposed by the court on a natural person convicted of the same offence.
@ref s 4B(3) (src:4377)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the multiple of the natural person's maximum for a body corporate` MEANS 5

-- src:4377 | (3) Where a body corporate is convicted of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth, the court may, if the contrary intention does not appear and the court thinks fit, impose a pecuniary penalty not exceeding an amount equal to 5 times the amount of the maximum pecuniary penalty that could be imposed by the court on a natural person convicted of the same offence.
@ref s 4B(3) (src:4377)
GIVEN `the maximum pecuniary penalty for a natural person` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the amount equal to 5 times the natural person's maximum` IS
    `the multiple of the natural person's maximum for a body corporate` TIMES `the maximum pecuniary penalty for a natural person`

§§ `Summary dealing: the stated limits (ss 4J and 4JA)`

-- src:4419 | (a) where the offence is punishable by imprisonment for a period not exceeding 5 years—a sentence of imprisonment for a period not exceeding 12 months or a fine not exceeding 60 penalty units, or both; or
@ref s 4J(3)(a) (src:4419)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 4J(3)(a) the most months of imprisonment a court of summary jurisdiction may impose` MEANS 12

-- src:4419 | (a) where the offence is punishable by imprisonment for a period not exceeding 5 years—a sentence of imprisonment for a period not exceeding 12 months or a fine not exceeding 60 penalty units, or both; or
@ref s 4J(3)(a) (src:4419)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 4J(3)(a) the most penalty units of fine a court of summary jurisdiction may impose` MEANS 60

-- src:4420 | (b) where the offence is punishable by imprisonment for a period exceeding 5 years but not exceeding 10 years—a sentence of imprisonment for a period not exceeding 2 years or a fine not exceeding 120 penalty units, or both.
@ref s 4J(3)(b) (src:4420)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 4J(3)(b) the most months of imprisonment a court of summary jurisdiction may impose` MEANS 2 TIMES `the number of months in a year`

-- src:4420 | (b) where the offence is punishable by imprisonment for a period exceeding 5 years but not exceeding 10 years—a sentence of imprisonment for a period not exceeding 2 years or a fine not exceeding 120 penalty units, or both.
@ref s 4J(3)(b) (src:4420)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 4J(3)(b) the most penalty units of fine a court of summary jurisdiction may impose` MEANS 120

-- src:4421 | (4) A court of summary jurisdiction may, if it thinks fit, upon the request of the prosecutor, hear and determine any proceeding in respect of an indictable offence against a law of the Commonwealth if the offence relates to property whose value does not exceed $5,000.
@ref s 4J(4) (src:4421)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the value of property, in dollars, that an indictable offence may not exceed for s 4J(4)` MEANS 5000

-- src:4422 | (5) Subject to subsection (6), where an offence is dealt with by a court of summary jurisdiction under subsection (4), the court may impose a sentence of imprisonment for a period not exceeding 12 months or a fine not exceeding 60 penalty units, or both.
@ref s 4J(5) (src:4422)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 4J(5) the most months of imprisonment a court of summary jurisdiction may impose` MEANS 12

-- src:4422 | (5) Subject to subsection (6), where an offence is dealt with by a court of summary jurisdiction under subsection (4), the court may impose a sentence of imprisonment for a period not exceeding 12 months or a fine not exceeding 60 penalty units, or both.
@ref s 4J(5) (src:4422)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 4J(5) the most penalty units of fine a court of summary jurisdiction may impose` MEANS 60

-- src:4435 | (b) the pecuniary penalty for the offence is not more than 600 penalty units for an individual or 3,000 penalty units for a body corporate; and
@ref s 4JA(1) (src:4435)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 4JA(1)(b) the most penalty units for an individual` MEANS 600

-- src:4435 | (b) the pecuniary penalty for the offence is not more than 600 penalty units for an individual or 3,000 penalty units for a body corporate; and
@ref s 4JA(1) (src:4435)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 4JA(1)(b) the most penalty units for a body corporate` MEANS 3000

-- src:4438 | (a) not more than 60 penalty units for an individual or 300 penalty units for a body corporate if the offence would be punishable on indictment by a pecuniary penalty of not more than 300 penalty units for an individual or 1,500 penalty units for a body corporate; or
@ref s 4JA(2)(a) (src:4438)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 4JA(2)(a) the most penalty units the court may impose on an individual` MEANS 60

-- src:4438 | (a) not more than 60 penalty units for an individual or 300 penalty units for a body corporate if the offence would be punishable on indictment by a pecuniary penalty of not more than 300 penalty units for an individual or 1,500 penalty units for a body corporate; or
@ref s 4JA(2)(a) (src:4438)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 4JA(2)(a) the most penalty units the court may impose on a body corporate` MEANS 300

-- src:4438 | (a) not more than 60 penalty units for an individual or 300 penalty units for a body corporate if the offence would be punishable on indictment by a pecuniary penalty of not more than 300 penalty units for an individual or 1,500 penalty units for a body corporate; or
@ref s 4JA(2)(a) (src:4438)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 4JA(2)(a) the most penalty units on indictment for an individual` MEANS 300

-- src:4438 | (a) not more than 60 penalty units for an individual or 300 penalty units for a body corporate if the offence would be punishable on indictment by a pecuniary penalty of not more than 300 penalty units for an individual or 1,500 penalty units for a body corporate; or
@ref s 4JA(2)(a) (src:4438)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 4JA(2)(a) the most penalty units on indictment for a body corporate` MEANS 1500

-- src:4439 | (b) not more than 120 penalty units for an individual or 600 penalty units for a body corporate if the offence would be punishable on indictment by a pecuniary penalty of not more than 600 penalty units for an individual or 3,000 penalty units for a body corporate.
@ref s 4JA(2)(b) (src:4439)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 4JA(2)(b) the most penalty units the court may impose on an individual` MEANS 120

-- src:4439 | (b) not more than 120 penalty units for an individual or 600 penalty units for a body corporate if the offence would be punishable on indictment by a pecuniary penalty of not more than 600 penalty units for an individual or 3,000 penalty units for a body corporate.
@ref s 4JA(2)(b) (src:4439)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 4JA(2)(b) the most penalty units the court may impose on a body corporate` MEANS 600

-- src:4439 | (b) not more than 120 penalty units for an individual or 600 penalty units for a body corporate if the offence would be punishable on indictment by a pecuniary penalty of not more than 600 penalty units for an individual or 3,000 penalty units for a body corporate.
@ref s 4JA(2)(b) (src:4439)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 4JA(2)(b) the most penalty units on indictment for an individual` MEANS 600

-- src:4439 | (b) not more than 120 penalty units for an individual or 600 penalty units for a body corporate if the offence would be punishable on indictment by a pecuniary penalty of not more than 600 penalty units for an individual or 3,000 penalty units for a body corporate.
@ref s 4JA(2)(b) (src:4439)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 4JA(2)(b) the most penalty units on indictment for a body corporate` MEANS 3000

§§ `Continuing offences (s 4K)`

-- s 4K(2): a person commits an offence in respect of each day during which
-- the person refuses or fails to comply, including the day of a conviction or
-- any later day. The text does not say which day is the first day of the
-- failure (the day the period expired, or the day after), so the first
-- failing day is a fact the caller states, and both ends are counted.
-- src:4447 | (2) Where a refusal or failure to comply with a requirement referred to in subsection (1) is an offence against a law of the Commonwealth, a person commits an offence in respect of each day during which the person refuses or fails to comply with that requirement, including the day of a conviction for any such offence or any later day.
@ref s 4K(2) (src:4447)
GIVEN `the first day of the failure` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the failure` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the number of days in respect of each of which an offence is committed` IS
    IF Day `the last day of the failure` LESS THAN Day `the first day of the failure`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST ((Day `the last day of the failure` MINUS Day `the first day of the failure`) PLUS 1)

-- s 4K(4): the one penalty "shall not exceed the sum of the maximum penalties
-- that could be imposed if a separate penalty were imposed in respect of each
-- offence". The maxima are in one unit (penalty units, or months of
-- imprisonment); the sum adds them.
-- src:4449 | (4) If a person is convicted of 2 or more offences referred to in subsection (3), the court may impose one penalty in respect of both or all of those offences, but that penalty shall not exceed the sum of the maximum penalties that could be imposed if a separate penalty were imposed in respect of each offence.
@ref s 4K(4) (src:4449)
GIVEN `the maximum penalties of the separate offences` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the number of offences counted` IS
    CONSIDER `the maximum penalties of the separate offences`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN 1 PLUS `the number of offences counted` rest

-- src:4449 | (4) If a person is convicted of 2 or more offences referred to in subsection (3), the court may impose one penalty in respect of both or all of those offences, but that penalty shall not exceed the sum of the maximum penalties that could be imposed if a separate penalty were imposed in respect of each offence.
@ref s 4K(4) (src:4449)
GIVEN `the maximum penalties of the separate offences` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the sum of the maximum penalties of 2 or more offences` IS
    IF `the number of offences counted` `the maximum penalties of the separate offences` AT LEAST 2
    THEN JUST (sum `the maximum penalties of the separate offences`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `The ages of children (ss 4M and 4N)`

-- src:4453 | A child under 10 years old cannot be liable for an offence against a law of the Commonwealth.
@ref s 4M (src:4453)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 4M the age below which a child cannot be liable, in years` MEANS 10

-- src:4455 | (1) A child aged 10 years or more but under 14 years old can only be liable for an offence against a law of the Commonwealth if the child knows that his or her conduct is wrong.
@ref s 4N(1) (src:4455)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 4N(1) the age from which a child can be liable, in years` MEANS 10

-- src:4455 | (1) A child aged 10 years or more but under 14 years old can only be liable for an offence against a law of the Commonwealth if the child knows that his or her conduct is wrong.
@ref s 4N(1) (src:4455)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 4N(1) the age below which a child can only be liable if the child knows the conduct is wrong, in years` MEANS 14

-- The text does not say how the years of a child's age are counted. This
-- function counts completed years from a date of birth, a year being
-- completed on the anniversary of the birth. A person born on 29 February has
-- no anniversary on 28 February of a year that has no 29 February, and the
-- text does not say whether the anniversary falls on 28 February or on 1
-- March, so that one day is NOTHING.
-- src:4453 | A child under 10 years old cannot be liable for an offence against a law of the Commonwealth.
@ref s 4M (src:4453)
GIVEN `the day of birth` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the age is taken` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the age in completed years` IS
    BRANCH IF Day `the day on which the age is taken` LESS THAN Day `the day of birth` THEN NOTHING
           IF     DATE_DAY `the day of birth` EQUALS 29 AND DATE_MONTH `the day of birth` EQUALS 2
              AND DATE_DAY `the day on which the age is taken` EQUALS 28 AND DATE_MONTH `the day on which the age is taken` EQUALS 2
              AND NOT (`is leap year` (DATE_YEAR `the day on which the age is taken`)) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST ((DATE_YEAR `the day on which the age is taken` MINUS DATE_YEAR `the day of birth`) MINUS IF `the birthday has passed` THEN 0 ELSE 1)
    WHERE
        `the birthday has passed` MEANS
               DATE_MONTH `the day on which the age is taken` GREATER THAN DATE_MONTH `the day of birth`
            OR (DATE_MONTH `the day on which the age is taken` EQUALS DATE_MONTH `the day of birth`
                AND DATE_DAY `the day on which the age is taken` AT LEAST DATE_DAY `the day of birth`)
